# Documentation Consistency

Reports, skills, and rules must be consistently structured so every artifact
is instantly recognisable and machine-parseable.

## Report File Naming

Every file saved to `reports/` must follow:

```
{ReportType}-{Product}-{Release}-{YYYY-MM-DD}{-Variant}.{ext}
```

| Segment | Rules | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| `ReportType` | TitleCase, one of: `VP-Executive`, `Sprint`, `Detailed`, `KPI`, `Prediction`, `Weekly-Status`, `Release-Brief` | `VP-Executive` |
| `Product` | Uppercase product key (per D1) | `NDB`, `DataLens` |
| `Release` | Major.Minor, no dots replaced | `2.11` |
| `YYYY-MM-DD` | ISO date, always present | `2026-05-08` |
| `-Variant` | Optional. Only when multiple variants of the same type on the same day | `-Email`, `-LiveData` |
| `.ext` | `.md` for markdown, `.html` for email, `.json` for raw data | `.md` |

**Valid:**
```
VP-Executive-NDB-2.11-2026-05-08.md
VP-Executive-NDB-2.11-2026-05-08-Email.html
Weekly-Status-DataLens-X-2026-05-08.md
Sprint-NDB-2.11-2026-05-08.md
```

**Invalid:**
```
CrystalBall-Enhanced-VP-Report-2026-04-21.md   ← missing Product+Release
Comprehensive-VP-Report-NDB-2.11-2026-04-20    ← wrong ReportType prefix
VP-Executive-Report-NDB-2.11-...                ← "Report" is redundant
```

## Markdown Report Frontmatter

Every `.md` report must open with:

```markdown
---
report_type: VP-Executive | Sprint | Detailed | KPI | Prediction | Weekly-Status | Release-Brief
product: NDB
release: "2.11"
generated: YYYY-MM-DD
data_source: live | skill | manual
audience: vp | director | tpm | rm | feat | team | ic
---
```

The `audience` field is required (per **`persona-aware-output.mdc`**) and
drives presenter selection.

## Markdown Report Section Order

In this order; omit only if genuinely no data:

1. `## Executive Summary` — 3–5 bullets, no prose paragraphs
2. `## Release Health` — overall RAG with 1-line justification
3. `## Project Status` — per-project table or bullets
4. `## Risk Assessment` — ranked risks with owner + mitigation (per D15 risk-register shape)
5. `## Trending` — week-over-week delta (omit only if first report)
6. `## Action Items` — assignee + due date for each
7. `## Appendix` — raw counts, JQL, supplemental data (optional)

## HTML Email Report Requirements

- Self-contained (all CSS inline, no external stylesheets / fonts)
- Open with: `<!-- {ReportType} | {Product} | {Release} | {Date} -->`
- Max table width: `800px`
- No `localhost` or internal addresses in `src` / `href`
- Plain-text fallback `<div>` for HTML-stripping clients

## Skill File Standards (`.cursor/skills/*/SKILL.md`)

Required sections in this order. Extra sections are fine; missing required
ones are not.

```markdown
---
name: skill-name-in-kebab-case
description: One sentence. Active verb. Includes "Use when".
audience: optional — vp | director | tpm | rm | feat | team | ic
---

## When to Use This Skill
(2–4 bullet triggers. Specific user wording or context.)

## Quick Start
(Minimal working example — shortest path to a useful output.)

## Core Rules
(Non-negotiable constraints. Numbered list.)

## Output Format
(Exact structure of what this skill produces. Include a template.)

## Quality Validation
(Checklist the agent runs before declaring done.)
```

Description must use **active verbs** ("Generate...", "Fetch..."), not "This
skill is for..." or "A skill that helps...".

Do not introduce non-canonical section names. Fold into:

| Concept | Canonical section |
|---|---|
| When to invoke | `## When to Use This Skill` |
| The rules | `## Core Rules` |
| What output looks like | `## Output Format` |
| How to verify correctness | `## Quality Validation` |

## Commit Message Convention for Docs

Use the prefix `docs:` or `skill:` or `rule:`:

```
docs: add VP-Executive-NDB-2.11-2026-05-08.md live-data report
skill: update fetch-project-tickets with bulk query optimisation
rule: add citation-first-output for audit-trailed agent answers
```

Never use generic messages like `update`, `fix`, or `generate report`.

## Grandfathering

- Reports already in `reports/`: leave them. Only new files must comply.
- Existing skill sections: rename to canonical names in the same commit
  when you next edit a skill.
- Existing rule files: grandfathered; new rules follow this standard.
